ClamAV 1.5.4 compatibility patch for OpenSSL 4.0 opaque ASN1_TIME
===================================================================
upstream        ClamAV 1.5.4 libclamav/crypto.c, from the signed release asset
                clamav-1.5.4.tar.gz sha256 1af1117a228f1b5bc7fa91a0dabc37848a99e7d25188e9be8043332ce721dfd3
                (Cisco Talos detached signature over the same bytes, checked in the same build step)
target          libclamav/crypto.c
target-sha256-before  6cfefd0ca043a922ddfda11c364f4995daf8a12317ce22f6c839b8c95a069dcc
target-sha256-after   ca71242d214a659473bd0cb1e6083eb58f1a997006e2553ec4fb6f79aee234f0
defect          cl_ASN1_GetTimeT reads timeobj->data and timeobj->type directly. ASN1_TIME has been opaque since
                OpenSSL 1.1.0; with the 4.0.3 headers the development closure installs, gcc refuses the four reads
                that build e6e7efb6 hit at crypto.c:1769/1772/1780/1789 ("invalid use of incomplete typedef
                'ASN1_TIME'"), so libclamav cannot compile at all.
change          the same parse, fed from the public accessors: ASN1_STRING_length / ASN1_STRING_get0_data /
                ASN1_STRING_type, copied into a 32-byte local buffer. The year adjustment still rewrites the string
                it parses, now the copy, so parsing, refusals (NULL object, missing data, short value, unknown type,
                strptime failure) and the returned tm are unchanged; only the mutation of the caller's object and
                the direct struct reads disappear. No API change, no version string change, no dependency change.
application     infra/product-preview/native-clamav-patches/apply-pinned-patch.py, run by the stage's pinned
                python3.13 after the archive's sha256 and signature checks, with these two hashes as arguments.
===================================================================
